# Own-wording spells of Valda's Spire of Secrets (2024), chunk 3. TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Accelerate/Decelerate": ["Reaction: add 2d6 to the damage of an attack, or cut that damage by 2d6.",
 "Reaction when a creature within range is about to be hit by an attack. Pick one. Accelerate: the target takes an extra 2d6 damage of the attack's type. Decelerate: the target takes 2d6 less damage, to a minimum of 0. Higher-level slot: the 2d6 grows by 1d6 per slot level above 1."],
"After Image": ["Make an illusory double. When you are hit, a d6 of 3+ hits the double instead and ends it.",
 "You create an illusory double that mirrors your movements for 10 minutes. When a creature hits you with an attack roll while the double stands, roll a d6. On a 3 or higher the double is hit instead and is destroyed. The double ignores all other damage and effects. It reappears if you move 15 ft or more on your turn or take the Dodge action. Creatures that are Blinded or have Blindsight or Truesight are not affected."],
"Arcane Anomaly": ["A 30 ft Emanation where spells fizzle on a d6 of 5-6, wasting the action but not the slot.",
 "A 30-ft Emanation around you warps magic for up to 1 minute (Concentration). Whenever anyone casts a spell inside it, roll a d6. On a 5 or 6 the spell fails with no effect and the action, Bonus Action or Reaction used is wasted. A spell slot spent on that casting is not used up."],
"Blunder": ["Reaction: an attacker makes a WIS save or fumbles its weapon or falls Prone, hurting the attack.",
 "Reaction when a creature within 30 ft makes an attack. It makes a Wisdom save or suffers an effect of your choice. Fumble: it drops one object it holds, which lands up to 10 ft away in a space you pick. If that was the attacking weapon, it can make an Unarmed Strike for the triggering attack. Prat Fall: it falls Prone, and the Disadvantage from Prone applies to the triggering attack."],
"Cheat": ["Bonus Action: until your next turn ends, reroll checks for nonmagical games of skill and keep the new roll.",
 "Until the end of your next turn you can reroll any ability check made to play a nonmagical game of skill, and you must use the new roll. It can sway a game of poker but not a Deck of Many Things."],
"Conjure Cover": ["Conjure three 5 ft stone wall segments (AC 10, 30 HP each) that give cover for 1 hour.",
 "You raise a low cobblestone wall on the ground at a point you see within 10 ft. It is 18 in thick and made of three segments, each 5 ft long and 3 ft high, and every segment must touch another. A Medium or Small creature crouching behind it has cover. The wall can be hopped over at no extra movement cost. Each segment has AC 10 and 30 HP and crumbles at 0 HP. It lasts up to 1 hour (Concentration) or until all segments are gone."],
"Cryptogram": ["Send an 8 character note to a creature you know on your plane. Once per 24 hours per recipient.",
 "You send a small scroll to a creature you know that is on your plane of existence. The scroll appears in front of it, in its pocket or on something nearby. The message holds up to 8 characters, spaces included. You cannot send another scroll to the same recipient for 24 hours."],
"Curse of Binding": ["A target makes a CHA save or is bound within 30 ft of a point, dragged back and blocked from teleporting.",
 "You tie a creature or object to a point you see within 60 ft. A creature must pass a Charisma save or be cursed to stay within 30 ft of the point. If it starts its turn farther away, it must pass a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC or be dragged 60 ft toward the point. If it tries to teleport or travel between planes, it makes a Charisma save. On a failure the attempt fails and the spell or effect is wasted. On a success the curse ends. Lasts until dispelled. Ritual."],
"Dead Mist Lash": ["Ranged spell attack, 3d8 Necrotic. Pay 5, 10 or 15 HP for +1d8 per 5 paid.",
 "Make a ranged spell attack against a creature within 60 ft. On a hit it takes 3d8 Necrotic damage. You can also take 5, 10 or 15 Necrotic damage yourself, ignoring Resistance and Immunity, and add 1d8 to the spell's damage for every 5 you take, to a maximum of 10d8 total. Higher-level slot: +1d8 per slot level above 1."],
"Dire Warning": ["Receive a 6 word message from your future self. Cannot recast for 7 days or until you send it back.",
 "You get a message of up to 6 words from yourself in the future, warning of a serious threat or pointing to a rewarding path. The GM writes it. Once you learn why it was sent, you must perform a 10 minute ritual, doable during a Short or Long Rest, to send it back to your past self. If you get no message, you will never finish that ritual, perhaps because you die or are stopped. After casting, you cannot cast this again for 7 days or until you finish the ritual."],
"Ethereal Jaunt": ["Bonus Action: a willing creature slips into the Ethereal Plane until the start of your next turn.",
 "A willing creature you touch steps into the border of the Ethereal Plane until the start of your next turn. The spell ends at once if it is already there. On that plane it can only affect and be affected by creatures, objects and effects there. It sees the plane it left in gray, but only out to 60 ft. Creatures not on the Ethereal Plane cannot perceive or interact with it unless a feature allows. It can move in any direction, and moving up or down costs 1 extra ft per foot. When the spell ends it returns to the matching spot, and if occupied it is pushed to the nearest free space."],
"Face Swap": ["Mark a willing creature for 1 hour. As a Magic action, see, hear and speak through it.",
 "You place an invisible sigil on a willing creature you see within 30 ft. It lasts 1 hour. During that time you can take a Magic action to project your face onto the marked creature and see, hear and speak through it as if you stood in its space, using your own senses instead of its. You dismiss the effect with no action. Ritual."],
"Flawed Resurrection": ["Raise a Humanoid dead up to 10 days as intelligent Undead with 1 HP. Its max HP drops 1 per Long Rest.",
 "You touch a dead Humanoid that died no more than 10 days ago and revive it as an intelligent Undead with 1 HP. Mortal wounds close but lost body parts do not return. It becomes Undead, with Immunity to Poison damage and the Poisoned condition. It needs no food, drink, sleep or air, but must still rest 8 hours for a Long Rest. Each Long Rest permanently lowers its HP maximum by 1, restorable only by Greater Restoration. If it dies and is later hit by Resurrection or similar magic, it returns with its original type."],
"Free Throw": ["Hurl an object up to 5 lb at a target. DEX save, 5d4 Bludgeoning, half on a success.",
 "Pick an unworn, uncarried object of 5 lb or less within 30 ft. You launch it at a creature or point within 150 ft along a path you choose, bending around corners and obstacles. The target makes a Dexterity save, taking 5d4 Bludgeoning damage on a fail or half on a success. The target gets no benefit from cover on this save. Higher-level slot: +2d4 damage and +5 lb maximum weight per slot level above 1."],
"Gahoul's Glorious Gothic": ["Conjure a gothic manor with 50 Skeleton servants for 7 days. Cast weekly for a year to make it permanent.",
 "A rift opens within 1 mile and bricks assemble into a gothic estate: a manor in a 200 by 200 ft courtyard with a 10 ft iron fence. Creatures in the area are gently but firmly escorted out by specters. You design the floor plan, up to fifty 10-ft Cubes and five floors, with barred windows and gargoyles. The layout is fixed once made. It holds food for 100 people for 7 days. Furnishings turn to smoke if taken past the perimeter. 50 Skeletons serve you and can do ordinary servant tasks but cannot attack or directly harm anyone. A Humanoid buried in the courtyard rises 24 hours later as a Ghoul under your control, up to 10 at once. They patrol if given no orders. Created Undead die if they leave the estate. When the spell ends the manor is pulled back into the rift. Cast it in the same place every 7 days for 365 days and it becomes permanent and cannot be dispelled. Casting time 1 hour."],
"Game of Fate": ["Compel a creature to a nonmagical game. The loser takes 6d6 Psychic. Wagers are binding.",
 "A creature within 60 ft that can hear and understand you is compelled into a nonmagical game with real stakes. An unwilling creature makes a Wisdom save to resist. The loser takes 6d6 Psychic damage. If nobody has won by the end of the 1 hour duration, you both take it. If you or an ally harms the target, you forfeit, and the same applies in reverse. You can wager more, up to 12d6 Psychic damage, as well as money, property or exotic prizes like a noble title. The spell shows if someone bets what they cannot pay. A bet is sealed by agreement and a handshake or similar. Wagered goods teleport to the winner and the loser is compelled to carry out wagered actions. Nothing but you and the target can influence the outcome. Ritual."],
"Halo of Flame": ["A 5 ft Emanation of fire. DEX save, 2d8 Fire, half on a success, once per turn per creature.",
 "A ring of flame ignites over your head and heats a 5-ft Emanation around you for up to 1 minute (Concentration). When the Emanation enters a creature's space you see, or a creature you see enters it or ends its turn there, you can force a Dexterity save. It takes 2d8 Fire damage on a fail or half on a success. A creature makes this save only once per turn. Higher-level slot: +1d8 per slot level above 2."],
"Hex: Bleeding": ["CON save or take extra 1d4 Necrotic on each damage taken (1d6 if Bloodied) until your next turn ends.",
 "A creature you see within 60 ft makes a Constitution save. On a fail, until the end of your next turn, each time it takes damage it takes an extra 1d4 Necrotic. If it is Bloodied, the extra is 1d6 instead."],
"Hex: Disorient": ["WIS save or -1d4 to attack rolls until your next turn ends. Die grows with level.",
 "A creature you see within 60 ft makes a Wisdom save. On a fail it subtracts 1d4 from its attack rolls until the end of your next turn. The die becomes 1d6 at level 5, 1d8 at level 11 and 1d10 at level 17."],
"Hex: Fortune": ["Touch a willing creature. It has Advantage on saving throws until your next turn ends.",
 "You touch a willing creature. Until the end of your next turn it has Advantage on saving throws."],
"Hex: Imperil": ["CON save or lose Resistance to a chosen damage type (Immunity becomes Resistance) until your next turn ends.",
 "You point at a creature you see within 60 ft and name a damage type. It makes a Constitution save. On a fail it loses Resistance to that type, or if it has Immunity it has only Resistance instead. This lasts until the end of your next turn."],
"Hex: Obfuscate": ["A 20 ft Emanation of fog, Heavily Obscured, until your next turn ends.",
 "You release fog in a 20-ft Emanation from you. It bends around corners and makes the area Heavily Obscured. It lasts until the end of your next turn or until strong wind such as Gust of Wind clears it, which ends the spell."],
"Hex: Stupor": ["WIS save or Incapacitated until your next turn ends. Ends on damage. Immune 24 hours after.",
 "A creature you see within 10 ft makes a Wisdom save. On a fail it is Incapacitated until the end of your next turn. The effect ends if it takes damage or if someone within 5 ft spends an action to shake it free. When the spell ends on a target, that target is immune to it for 24 hours."],
"Hex: Ward": ["Touch: the target takes 2 less damage from each hit until your next turn ends. Grows with level.",
 "You touch a willing creature. Until the end of your next turn, each time it takes damage that damage is reduced by 2. The reduction becomes 3 at level 5, 4 at level 11 and 5 at level 17."],
"Icicle Javelin": ["Ranged spell attack, 3d8 Cold. If the target is next to a wall its Speed is 0 until your next turn.",
 "You hurl a huge icicle at a creature within 60 ft with a ranged spell attack. On a hit it takes 3d8 Cold damage. If it is also next to a wall or similar fixed object, its Speed is 0 until the start of your next turn. Higher-level slot: +1d8 per slot level above 1."],
"Inexorable Sarcophagus": ["DEX save or a Large or smaller creature is trapped in a sarcophagus. Three failed saves crush it for 100.",
 "You throw a palm-sized sarcophagus at a Large or smaller creature you see within 30 ft. It makes a Dexterity save as the coffin grows to full size. On a fail the target is Blinded and Incapacitated, its Speed is 0 and it has cover from outside effects, for up to 1 minute (Concentration). The sarcophagus is an object of the target's size with AC 15, 100 HP and Immunity to Poison and Psychic. At 0 HP the spell ends. The target repeats the Dexterity save at the end of each of its turns, keeping track of successes and failures separately. Three successes free it and end the spell. Three failures and the sarcophagus crushes it for 100 Bludgeoning damage. A creature killed by this spell rises at the start of your next turn as a Mummy that obeys your spoken orders."],
"Invisibility Purge": ["A 120 ft Emanation strips invisibility for 1 minute. Invisible creatures make a CON save or are Stunned.",
 "You burst out magic in a 120-ft Emanation around you. Each Invisible creature and object inside is outlined with a magical aura and cannot benefit from the Invisible condition for 1 minute. An affected creature must pass a Constitution save or be Stunned until the start of your next turn."],
"Legendary Libation": ["Bonus Action: fill a container with a drink giving 1d6 Temp HP and Advantage on saves against Frightened.",
 "A container of your choice within 30 ft fills with a drink such as ale or tea. Drinking it takes a Bonus Action or Utilize action. The drinker gains 1d6 Temporary HP and Advantage on saves to avoid or end the Frightened condition. These benefits last until the start of its next turn. An undrunk drink vanishes at the start of your next turn. The Temporary HP die becomes 2d6 at level 5, 3d6 at level 11 and 4d6 at level 17."],
"Mandy's Feral Follower": ["Turn Medium or smaller Beasts into Commoner allies in Fine Clothes with 10 Temp HP until midnight.",
 "You touch a Medium or smaller Beast within 30 ft. It becomes a Humanoid with an appearance you choose. Its stats are replaced with those of a Commoner, but it keeps its HP and Hit Dice. You pick its skill proficiency. It wears Fine Clothes with no other gear and can handle basic unskilled tasks. It gains 10 Temporary HP, and the spell ends on it early when those are gone. When it ends, the clothes turn to smoke. It is your ally and your allies', rolls its own Initiative, acts on its own turn and behaves as your employee. Duration: where time passes normally, until the twelfth stroke of the next midnight. Elsewhere, 24 hours. Higher-level slot: one more Beast per slot level above 4."],
"Memorize": ["Glance at a page and recall it exactly for a year, then with Advantage on Intelligence checks.",
 "You scan a page of writing and commit it to memory. For the next year you recall every detail on it. After that you have Advantage on Intelligence checks to recall the information. Ritual."],
"Nondescript": ["For 1 hour, those who see or hear you cannot recall your looks or voice.",
 "You become unremarkable, though your real appearance does not change. For 1 hour, creatures that see or hear you cannot recall how you look or sound."],
"Phantasmal Beauty": ["WIS save or the target is Charmed, Incapacitated and stuck. Each save it passes deals 4d10 Psychic and ends it.",
 "You conjure a vision of a creature's deepest desires within 120 ft, visible only to it. It makes a Wisdom save. On a fail it is Charmed and Incapacitated with Speed 0 for up to 1 minute (Concentration). It repeats the save whenever it takes damage and at the end of each of its turns. On a success it takes 4d10 Psychic damage and the spell ends. Higher-level slot: +1d10 per slot level above 3."],
"Polybrachia": ["A willing creature grows two extra arcane arms. Advantage on Athletics and a Bonus Action weapon attack.",
 "Two strong arms of arcane energy appear on a willing creature you touch, for up to 10 minutes (Concentration). They work like real arms: they can hold weapons and Shields, so the target can hold two two-handed or four one-handed weapons at once, perform Somatic components, and so on. The target has Advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks and can use a Bonus Action to make a melee attack with a weapon held by the arms."],
"Proto-Conjuration": ["A 20 ft radius Sphere: fog (L1), hazards (L2+) or grasping vines (L3+). Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "You create an obstacle filling a 20-ft-radius Sphere centered on a point within 60 ft, for up to 1 minute (Concentration). Pick one. Obscured: the Sphere is Heavily Obscured by fog, foliage or heavy rain. Hazardous (level 2+ slot): Difficult Terrain full of thorns, spikes or icicles. Each creature there makes a Dexterity save when it appears, on its first entry each turn and when it ends its turn there, once per turn, taking Piercing damage of 1d6 per slot level on a fail or half on a success. Grasping (level 3+ slot): Difficult Terrain full of vines, tentacles or webs. A creature that enters it for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there makes a Strength save or is Restrained. A Restrained creature can use an action for a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC to break free."],
"Proto-Illusion": ["Create an illusion up to a 15 ft Cube for 10 minutes. Higher slots add sound, solidity, then damage.",
 "You create an illusion of an object, creature or visible phenomenon no larger than a 15-ft Cube at a spot within 60 ft, for up to 10 minutes (Concentration). As a Magic action you can move it within range and adjust its look. Anything touching it passes through and reveals it. A creature that takes the Study action can make an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC to see through it. If it does, the illusion's other qualities fade for it. Pick one add-on. Silent: only visual. Realistic (level 3+ slot): adds fitting sound, smell and temperature but cannot damage or inflict conditions. Tangible (level 4+): Realistic and solid, so touching it no longer reveals it. It has AC 15 and 1 HP and vanishes at 0, and you can make it reappear with a Bonus Action, though creatures that saw it vanish can tell it is fake. Damaging (level 5+): Realistic and Tangible, and as a Bonus Action you force a creature within 60 ft of it to make an Intelligence save, taking 4d8 Psychic on a fail or half on a success. A creature that has seen through it has Advantage on that save."],
"Quickstep": ["Bonus Action: +10 ft Speed until the start of your next turn.",
 "A burst of speed. Your Speed increases by 10 ft until the start of your next turn."],
"Ruby-Eye Curse": ["CON save or a creature is Blinded beyond 5 ft for up to 10 minutes.",
 "A red haze clouds the eyes of a creature within 30 ft that meets your gaze. It makes a Constitution save or is cursed for up to 10 minutes (Concentration). While cursed it sees normally within 5 ft but is Blinded beyond that."],
"Sanction": ["Bonus Action: a CON save or a target is marked. When you take damage, it takes 1d8 Necrotic or Radiant.",
 "You fling a drop of blood at a creature you see within 30 ft. It makes a Constitution save or is marked for up to 1 hour (Concentration). Each time you take damage, the marked creature takes 1d8 Necrotic or Radiant damage, your choice. The spell ends early if you end your turn more than 30 ft from the target."],
"Shriek": ["Bonus Action: push Large or smaller creatures you choose in a 5 ft Emanation 5 ft away.",
 "You let out a blood-chilling screech in a 5-ft Emanation. Each Large or smaller creature you choose in it is pushed 5 ft away from you."],
"Soul Effigy": ["CON save binds a Humanoid's soul to a doll for 8 hours. Magic action: control it, deal 2d8, or Restrain it.",
 "A Humanoid you touch makes a Constitution save. On a fail a piece of its soul binds to the doll used in the casting, which becomes its effigy. The spell ends if the effigy is destroyed or the target is on another plane. Lasts 8 hours. Casting time 1 minute. Ritual. As a Magic action you choose one. Control: you direct the target's next turn through the effigy's limbs. It can only Dash, Disengage, Hide or Utilize, and moves jerkily. Harm: you prod the effigy and the target takes 2d8 damage of a type fitting the method, ignoring Resistance and Immunity. Restrain: you dunk the effigy in water, and the target believes it is suffocating and is Restrained until the end of your next turn."],
"Sulfuric Smoke": ["A 5 ft Cube of acid smoke. CON save or 1d8 Acid. Creatures fully inside have Disadvantage on attacks.",
 "You make a 5-ft Cube of acidic smoke at a point you see within 60 ft. Each creature in it makes a Constitution save or takes 1d8 Acid damage. The area is Lightly Obscured and lasts until the start of your next turn. A creature entirely inside has Disadvantage on attack rolls. Damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17."],
"Sword of Judgment": ["A 20 ft Sphere of spectral swords. When a creature inside attacks or casts, DEX save or 4d8 Force.",
 "You mark a 20-ft-radius Sphere centered within 60 ft, for up to 1 minute (Concentration). A spectral sword hangs over each creature inside and follows it while it stays. Whenever a creature in the Sphere makes an attack or casts a spell, you can force it to make a Dexterity save before the attack or spell resolves. On a fail it takes 4d8 Force damage, or half on a success. A creature makes this save only once per turn. Higher-level slot: +1d8 per slot level above 5."],
"Transient Bulwark": ["For 8 hours, the next attack roll against you has a -10 penalty and the spell ends.",
 "An invisible, fragile shield guards you for 8 hours. The next attack roll made against you takes a -10 penalty, and then the spell ends. Ritual."],
"Winter Flower": ["Plant a Tiny flower that explodes for 10d8 Cold in a 30 ft Emanation (DEX save, half on a success).",
 "A Tiny white flower sprouts at a point on the ground within 120 ft. It has AC 15, 1 HP, Vulnerability to Fire and Immunity to Cold and Psychic. For 24 hours you can use a Bonus Action to detonate it, and it also explodes if reduced to 0 HP. Each creature within a 30-ft Emanation of the flower makes a Dexterity save, taking 10d8 Cold damage on a fail or half on a success. If it does not explode within the duration it withers. Casting this on the same spot daily for 7 days makes it last until dispelled."],
"Word of Terror": ["Bonus Action: WIS save or 2d6 Psychic and Frightened until your next turn ends. Half damage on a success.",
 "You speak a word of fear to a creature you see within 30 ft. It makes a Wisdom save. On a fail it takes 2d6 Psychic damage and is Frightened until the end of your next turn. On a success it takes half damage and nothing else. Higher-level slot: +1d6 per slot level above 2."],
}
